{
  "info": {
    "name": "Reni Social API",
    "description": "##  Quick Setup Pro-Tip (Do This First!)\n\nBefore testing any endpoints, click on the **Reni Social API** collection name in the left sidebar, go to the **Variables** tab, and set up these initial values so you don't have to type them manually every time:\n\n| Variable | Initial Value | Notes |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| `workspace_id` | `Your current workspace UUID |\n| `session_id` | *(your current redis session token)* | Get this from the `/api/auth/signin` response |\n| `token` | `dummy_token` | The middleware just checks for the word \"Bearer\" |\n| `attempt_id` | *(leave blank for now)* | Will be populated after triggering a publish |\n\n---\n\n# Reni Social API\n\n**Authentication:**\nProtected routes (under `/api/in`) require two headers:\n1. `Authorization: Bearer {{token}}` (Fiber middleware just checks for the word \"Bearer\")\n2. `X-Session-Id: {{session_id}}` (The actual session token from the `/api/auth/signin` response)\n\n**Workflows:**\nCheck the ** API Workflows \u0026 Guides** folder below for detailed frontend integration guides, including the Real-Time Async Publishing flow.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": " API Workflows \u0026 Guides",
      "description": "Documentation for complex multi-step workflows in the Reni Social API.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Real-Time Publishing Flow (Frontend Guide)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "http://127.0.0.1:1040/health",
              "host": [
                "http://127.0.0.1:1040"
              ],
              "path": [
                "health"
              ]
            },
            "description": "#  Real-Time Publishing Workflow\n\nWhen a user clicks \"Publish\", the backend processes platforms asynchronously (especially Instagram/TikTok videos, which can take 10–30 seconds to process on Meta's servers). Instead of blocking the UI with a long loading spinner, we use an **Idempotency Key + Smart Polling** approach.\n\n## The 3-Step Flow\n\n###  Trigger the Publish\n**Endpoint:** `POST /api/in/posts/in/:id/publish?workspace_id=:workspace_id`\n\nInstead of returning \"post published\", the API now immediately returns a tracking ID.\n\n**Response:**\n```json\n{\n    \"message\": \"publishing_initiated\",\n    \"attempt_id\": \"8f4e2d1c-9b3a-4e5f-8c7d-6e5f4a3b2c1d\"\n}\n```\n**Action:** Save the `attempt_id` in your component state. This is your \"receipt\" for this specific button click.\n\n---\n\n###  Poll for Real-Time Status\n**Endpoint:** `GET /api/in/posts/in/:id/results?attempt_id=:attempt_id`\n\n**Action:** Start a `setInterval` (every 2 seconds) calling this endpoint using the `attempt_id` from Step 1. Because we pass the `attempt_id`, the API will ignore any old failed attempts and only return the status of the *current* publish job.\n\n**Response:**\n```json\n{\n    \"results\": [\n        {\n            \"platform\": \"linkedin\",\n            \"status\": \"published\",\n            \"platform_post_id\": \"urn:li:share:7123...\",\n            \"fail_reason\": \"\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"platform\": \"meta_ig\",\n            \"status\": \"processing\",\n            \"container_id\": \"17954...\",\n            \"fail_reason\": \"\"\n        }\n    ]\n}\n```\n**UI Mapping:**\n* `status === 'processing'`  Show a spinner for that specific platform.\n* `status === 'published'`  Show a green checkmark.\n* `status === 'failed'`  Show a red X and display the `fail_reason`.\n\n---\n\n###  Stop Polling (Terminal State)\n**Action:** Check if **all** platforms in the `results` array have reached a terminal state (`published` or `failed`). Once they have, clear the interval.\n\n```javascript\nconst allDone = results.every(r =\u003e r.status === 'published' || r.status === 'failed');\nif (allDone) {\n    clearInterval(pollingInterval);\n}\n```\n"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
